  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "I've been finding recently that I want to be able to switch between a couple different face options for some avatars, while retaining the smoothness of viseme blendshapes. Doing this through the SDK, however, proves very troublesome. One rather simple option would be to expose a parameter for viseme blendshape weight, which would allow custom viseme animations to replicate the smoothness of blendshape-based viseme animations.\n\nThe viseme parameter is great but it doesn't provide enough information to recreate the smooth lip-sync in complex situations, where you cannot just set the blendshapes in the descriptor. You can't even have other parameter-based visemes unless you can hide the changing main blendshapes.",
